WEBVTT

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:04.830
Hold it.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.540
Takemitsu Shinzou, I presume.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.190
Who goes there?

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.240
What do you think you're 
doing in that outfit?

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.840
I'm sure you are aware of the 
school uniform regulations.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.930
Oh, pardon!

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.070
This is the usual garb for a samurai...

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.180
Two-week suspension from 
extra-curricular activities!

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.420
You will submit a written 
letter of apology by tomorrow!

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.530
You art no teacher, and thus have 
no right to pronounce such things!

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.170
If you have a problem with my beliefs,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.680
then we'll settle this by arms!

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.140
I don't know your "policies" or whatever.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.020
The teachers here are lax about the 
rules, but I won't let this slide.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.680
I'm a member of the Student Council!

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.030
I have all the rights I need.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:30.370
<b>Episode 5: The Ghost of the Incinerator</b>

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.510
<b>Now Saving {Yes, I'm subtitling the horrible engrish into something comprehensible :) }</b>

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.150
Huh? The Spider Society?

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.760
<b>Sket-dan
Now accepting requests</b>

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:44.680
Yes. They seem to be an underground group

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.270
that has been blackmailing 
students from this area.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.300
Underground, huh?

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.270
The heck? Someone should 
catch these guys, and quick.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:58.260
However, as the victims won't give their 
names, the crimes aren't coming to light.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.360
<b>Information Requested about the Spider Society</b>

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.360
Even their existence hasn't been 
proven to be more than a rumor.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.670
What a bunch of lies!

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.110
You hear urban legends 
like this all the time.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.140
Oh yeah, today's Wednesday.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.410
<b>Throw out trash to the incinerator
Monday, Wednesday, Friday!</b>

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.720
It's your turn, Himeko.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.170
Go throw out the trash.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.170
<b>On Trash Duty</b>

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.920
I d-don't want to!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:14.680
Huh?

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:17.020
Hey, come on... We can only take 
out the trash every other...

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.360
I said no!

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.870
Fine, then.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.110
Switch, I'll give you 100 yen if you...

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:22.900
Understood!

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.540
Sheesh, you're cheap. I was just kidding.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.240
It's not like you to go against the rules.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.200
Just go and do it, okay?

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.250
Absolutely no way!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.580
But, why?

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.820
Because there's a... a...

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.780
There's a ghost!

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.210
A-A-A-A-A...

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.380
A ghost!

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.310
Oh hi, Yuuki-san.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.820
What, you know her?

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.580
Accept it...

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.270
There are ghosts...

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.460
For real...

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:05.970
Switch-kun, today, yes today, 
I will have you realize it...

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.530
She's coming!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.260
Please don't come in like that!

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.320
She is Yuuki Reiko-san, a 
member of the Occult Club.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.220
#31 in class 2-A.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.540
She has deep knowledge of all dubious 
subjects, such as ghosts, ESP, curses, and the like.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.790
I once got into a scuffle with her 
over whether or not ghosts exist.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.850
W-What were you thinking?

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.540
You never change, Switch-kun.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.580
You still wander around, unable to 
break out of the bounds of "science".

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.810
Lord Satan must be laughing!

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:42.010
Scary!

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.750
I do not desire to resume 
our war of words here.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:50.320
I'd rather not see you groveling before 
me, at a loss after your crushing defeat.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.850
Silence, you!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.560
Heaven will punish you!

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.230
I wanna go home...

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.670
Ēloïm, Ēloïm, Essaïm...

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.480
So, I came to talk about this incident today.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.230
Huh? The Ghost of the Incinerator?

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.760
It is one of the seven 
mysteries of this academy.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:07.180
There is a column in the Academy Times 
which introduces them one at a time.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.770
Oh, there is?

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:14.250
But sheesh... Today, first it's those 
"spiders" and now it's another fishy story...

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.580
Ten years ago!

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.870
A male student, a nervous 
wreck from entrance exams...

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:28.130
Don't go using my voice to put in 
unneeded sound effects, Switch!

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.570
But somehow, he didn't die.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:34.940
Almost by instinct, he lumbered, barely 
conscious, toward the incinerator.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.150
But it was locked that day, and 
he couldn't open the gate...

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.440
He wasn't able to get inside, and when 
he was discovered the next morning...

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.240
I said, stop using me for 
your reenactment film!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.930
Ever since then, at that very location...

00:05:53.210 --> 00:06:00.520
There have been witnesses claiming they've 
seen a ghost hovering over the flower beds.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:03.040
Exactly like this.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.290
Ghost?

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.540
Let's have at 'im!

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.820
I'll give him a taste of 
my special knuckle p-punch!

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.140
...you say when you're shaking like a leaf!

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.420
Shut up!

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:18.560
Is this the reason you didn't want 
to go throw out the trash before?

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.780
Ooh, looky here! The almighty Onihime's 
actually got a cute side to her!

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.980
Oww!

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:28.740
It hurts! It really hurts! I mean, 
seriously, man, it hurts! Come on!

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.740
Bossun, you fool... You fool...

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:30.290
Foolishness!

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.570
There are no such things 
as ghosts in this world!

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:35.830
I only believe in reality which 
is backed up by hard data!

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.420
It's only a matter of time before 
that smirk is wiped off your face.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.030
Why, you ask?

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.010
Because the one who took that picture...

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.870
...was none other than myself!

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:52.100
Yes... It was last Tuesday...

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.860
I was staked out nearby, after taking 
interest in the article in the Academy Times,

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:00.230
thinking I could perhaps take 
a picture of the ghost...

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.690
And then...

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.650
Wait, <i>you</i> were scared, too?

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:15.320
Then, as if in a daze...

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:20.060
I brought the camera to the Newspaper 
Club, and this is the result.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:25.050
So? Now do you believe in 
the existence of ghosts?

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.300
This argument is truly pointless.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.840
But, say I found a witness 
who contradicted you...

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.580
Sounds interesting.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.670
But can you, I wonder?

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:38.430
Can you, Sket-dan?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.270
I'm out! I want no part of this!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.210
And you two, stop fighting!

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.050
Then I request this of the Sket-dan:

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:51.380
Investigate the Ghost of the Incinerator and 
explain the truth behind what I witnessed!

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.440
But, like I said...

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.530
We don't want to be a part of this.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.660
We accept!

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:55.840
Hey!

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.680
Don't just decide things 
like that, you idiot!

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:58.970
I'm the leader, remember?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.760
What's wrong with you? I'm 
gonna destroy that computer!

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.790
Don't worry, I'll do the 
investigation myself.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.040
Information gathering is my specialty.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:10.950
Fascinating!

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:14.850
Then, I will go get even more proof!

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.020
You're on!

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.370
I gladly accept!

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:18.200
Duel!

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.550
Wait, do they...

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:21.810
...actually get along really well?

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:29.110
"Come to this place after 
school tomorrow, alone."

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.170
"If you don't, we'll spread 
this picture around."

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:33.470
...so that's how it is?

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.170
And, why are we tailing him?

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.370
<b>Our Nervous Hearts are One! Our Nervous Fight Will Save the World!</b>

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.370
<b>Every Sunday at 8:30 AM on TV Souchou!
Everyone please watch!!</b>

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:42.030
Don't you think this is gonna be interesting?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.370
Aren't you curious about 
how he's gonna gather info?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:45.540
If her skirt was like, 2 cm 
higher, I could almost see,

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.410
but after I got my camera ready, 
her manager jumped in front...

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.410
Spying on our friends is excitin', you know?

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.630
Not really.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.930
Maybe another time.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:51.880
Oh, sure I know Miss Yuuki Reiko.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.380
She might be in a different field, 
but she and I are both hard-core.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.860
I can feel a common bond between us.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.140
Like we're both newtypes...

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.420
Personally, I'm quite convinced 
she's one of those archetypes

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:03.150
where, when you put some makeup on her 
natural face, she instantly changes completely!

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.660
Plus, someone like me who 
loves long black hair moe,

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.650
I really wish she'd cosplay as a goth loli.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:11.650
Goth would suit her so well, wouldn't 
it push her even farther away from moe?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.710
It'd totally be moe!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.760
I can't believe there's anyone who 
wouldn't get excited by goth lolis!

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:14.540
G-Got loli?

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.510
He's got lollipops?

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.160
Anyway, getting back to the point...

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.460
Right, the Newspaper Club.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:22.410
A girl named Shimada-san 
there is Miss Yuuki's friend.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.110
2-F, Shimada Takako.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:26.910
The hot-blooded reporter from the 
Newspaper Club who loves a scoop.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.690
Yes, that's her.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.230
Now that I think about it, she'd 
be perfect for a nurse outfit...

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.920
Got it. Thank you very much.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:33.950
Some other time, then.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.280
By the way, Mr. Usui...

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.890
Did you get that thing I asked for?

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.680
Of course. There is nothing I cannot find.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.930
<b>Limited Edition</b>

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.930
Yes! This is it!

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.940
The limited edition figure of 
Futari wa Nervous's Marriage Blue

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:49.350
and Maternity Blue's Ultimate form!

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:50.940
Mr. Usui, you're awesome!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:51.960
Bingo.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:55.060
In exchange, I'm counting on you to help the 
next time I need information about the school.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:57.910
Sure thing! I'll be glad to help. Nya!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:58.900
Yes, yes...

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:58.900
He said "nya".

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.170
I heard it the first time...

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:05.540
<b>Newspaper Club
Let's Read!</b>

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:06.550
That's right, I'm the one in charge of the 
"seven mysteries of the academy" column.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:10.650
Well, it's not a big column, so honestly, 
there hasn't been much reaction to it.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:13.040
But Reiko at least seems 
to have taken an interest.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.580
Yuuki-san brought you that picture, yes?

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:17.210
Yeah...

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:22.880
I told Reiko to go around with a camera searching for 
mysteries, and if something happened, to bring it to me.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:29.730
Once I took a look at the data, 
it was such a great shot!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:36.080
Anyway, I hear quite a lot of talk 
about you going around, Usui-kun.

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:42.280
Like, how you're handsome and know 
everything, and are a really interesting person.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.060
Thank you.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:45.710
Can I interview you for 
the newspaper next time?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:45.710
No, thank you!

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.030
Then, when can I?

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:49.980
120,000,000 years from now.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.600
What's with that?

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:54.170
You'll likely give up after 8000 years.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.500
Switch is actually pretty popular.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:58.340
Just as reticent as ever, you are...

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:58.340
For some reason, I can't forgive 
him for that from deep within!

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:02.340
Now that I think about it, there 
are rumors Yoshi also saw a ghost.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.380
By that you mean Shimizu Yoshie-san?

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.810
No. The one that's my classmate.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:07.960
Yoshinari-kun?

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:10.880
I definitely saw it-nari.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.400
That was without a doubt a spirit manifested 
in this world... In other words, a ghost-nari!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.160
It was silently hovering above the flower 
beds with both feet off the ground-nari.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.980
Then, suddenly, everything was 
covered in light from the sunset,

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:25.330
and I got out of there 
as fast as I could-nari!

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:26.100
That punch perm must be 
makin' Yoshi punch-drunk!

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.360
Seriously?

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:30.250
All of the guy's friends 
are complete weirdos...

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.290
When was this, exactly?

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:36.000
It was last week, on Wednesday evening-nari.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.960
I remember it well. It was when I went to 
take out the trash for the Calligraphy Club-nari.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:43.300
I see. Thank you very much.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:51.630
Ooh, I got mail!

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:52.980
Why now, of all times?

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.600
Got time to kill?

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:57.780
I know you've been tailing me.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.410
He's looking this way!

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.020
Damn it!

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:03.230
God damn him... He pisses me off.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:12.920
So in the end, I only found two witnesses: 
Yuuki-san and Yoshinari-cchi.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:17.620
When I consider the spread of the rumors, 
I think there might be others...

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:21.040
What's with you? Are you angry or something?

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.580
Enough!

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.530
Ghosts exist, I knew it!

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:27.130
Stop this stupid fighting and 
hurry up and exorcise it!

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.070
I'm gonna make you guys 
disappear from this world!

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.580
What did I do?!

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.120
Don't worry, it's just 
everyone being mistaken.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.280
And Switch being popular is 
also everyone being mistaken!

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.920
Take a look at this picture!

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.520
How do you explain it?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.530
How is it just floating there?!

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.400
If you can float, then 
float for me right now!

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.830
Sure I can float... My head's in the 
clouds during class all the time.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.200
You can stay up there the 
rest of your life, damn you!

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.750
Just calm down, okay?

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.880
Leave the picture for now...

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.630
What is it, Bossun?

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:56.540
Hold it a sec...

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:00.090
They're on!

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.850
You okay?

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.060
Switch, look something up for me.

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:17.900
I know the identity of the ghost!

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:20.080
Next: Bosun's Hint!

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.110
The incinerator!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:22.610
This is plagiarism!

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:25.980
Do you believe, or not?

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:27.950
Whoa! That's going too far!

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.790
<b>The next day, Thursday</b>

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.010
What are you doing here?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.490
What, you ask?

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:43.640
I thought the ghost might 
appear again if I waited here.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:46.830
I see. Then, why don't we wait together?

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.050
We'll wait for the ghost 
that will soon appear.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.530
I see...

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:59.700
So, about when did you see the ghost, Yoshi?

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:01.150
It appeared!

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.780
The ghost appeared in 
front of the incinerator!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.160
What? It did?!

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.050
Narinari?!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.490
I-I-It's here! It's actually here!

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.060
T-Take a look, Switch-kun!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:15.460
A ghost?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:16.200
Over there...

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:20.770
It's floating!

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.340
But that can't be!

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:24.360
That can't be, you say?

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.920
You mean you didn't believe 
the article you wrote?

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:30.110
It spoke...

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:33.590
The true identity of the ghost is you...

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:34.930
Shimada Takako!

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:40.080
Takako? What's going on?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.380
Weren't you just floating in the air?

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.090
It's a trick.

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:48.070
Although it takes a little setup, 
it's an illusion anyone can do.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:53.780
You cut a slit through one of your pant 
legs, so that you can stick your leg out.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:58.040
<b>Side!</b>

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:58.040
<b>Rear!</b>

00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:58.040
Then it looks like you're 
floating from the back.

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:06.090
FYI, Switch made these last night!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.810
Wow, that's impressive!

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.130
H-Hey, wait a second!

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:15.180
I had no idea! I mean, who 
could tell a trick like that...

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.380
It's not just the trick!

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.290
I noticed there was something 
wrong with the picture!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:23.100
See? The gate is open in the 
picture that was in the newspaper.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.940
But that lock is only open 
Monday, Wednesday, and Friday.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:33.400
Which means this isn't the picture 
that Yuuki-san took on Tuesday!

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.620
Plus...

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.160
That's the camera from before...

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.470
Right. You borrowed it from 
the Newspaper Club, right?

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.440
I asked them a favor and they let me take it.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.170
Your pictures were all blurry 
and couldn't be used.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.170
You were taking them while 
extremely frightened, after all.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:54.520
That's why you retook them the next 
day using the self-timer, Shimada!

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:58.430
The ghost that Yoshi saw 
was Shimada that day.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:01.100
The light was the flash, I bet.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.810
Takako... It was you?

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:15.990
I always wanted to write 
a front-page scoop...

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:23.040
My articles were always pushed into the 
corner, and no one ever talked about them...

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:28.450
But Reiko... She really got 
into my seven mysteries column.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:33.080
Plus, she loves the occult, so I 
couldn't help but give it a shot...

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.670
G-Ghost?!

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.890
Yeah! I hear there are people 
that actually witnessed it!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.820
Right about five in the evening...

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:41.680
Camera... Where's a camera?!

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:46.170
I didn't plan on deceiving her at first.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:50.330
But when I saw her like that, I just 
got pulled more and more along...

00:16:57.110 --> 00:17:03.310
Since you couldn't use the pictures that 
Yuuki-san took, you retook them yourself.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.570
I'm sorry, Reiko.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.290
I'm really, really...

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:17.490
I will never forgive!!

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.660
There she goes!

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.010
...is what I want to say, but...

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:24.970
Fine. Let's let bygones by bygones.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.580
Reiko, thank you!

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.940
Oh hey, Reiko-san's a nice 
person! She's not scary at all!

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:35.450
If it were me I'd beat the 
living crap out of her!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.200
You're <i>way</i> too scary!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:41.280
Next time, I'll find a scoop 
all by myself, really!

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:49.130
Well, I also have times where I let my 
passion make me take things too far.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:54.010
Switch-kun...

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.200
I'll accept defeat, this time.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:18:00.500
I have been defeated by your information 
gathering skills, and the Sket-dan's teamwork.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:03.100
But one day I will make you accept it!

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.050
I'll pull you in!

00:18:05.050 --> 00:18:07.460
Drag you into the world of the occult!

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:08.730
Fine by me.

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:13.130
Then I will simply keep gathering 
information that contradicts you!

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:20.560
I think they get along.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:21.950
Let's leave 'em alone.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.280
Welcome to the Spider Society.

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:29.490
Kaimei Academy second-year, class D...

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:32.910
Dejima Kiku-chan, was it?

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:36.450
A newcomer of ours...

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:37.540
Hashiba.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:40.130
...has told us <i>all</i> about you.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.800
You are a butterfly caught in our web.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:47.010
If you resist, we'll spread this around.

00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:49.620
Which is better? Supplying us 
with a little pocket money,

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:54.270
or having your school life 
turn into a living hell?

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.480
I'm sure you know the answer...

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.240
Say something, hey!

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.880
So scared she can't speak, is it?

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:11.930
What's this?

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:12.910
Why, you...

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:16.840
W-Who are you?

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:22.510
I am the Vice President of Kaimei Academy's 
Student Council, second-year Tsubaki Sasuke!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:27.350
You have attempted a serious 
crime against our students.

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.980
I'll catch the lot of you here, all at once!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:33.880
What proof do you have?

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.300
If you resist, we'll spread this around.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.280
Which is better? Supplying us 
with a little pocket money...

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.400
Hand it over!

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:44.610
Don't you care what happens to this girl?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:47.950
My eyes!

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.780
Don't underestimate us!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:54.920
Y-You!

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:58.420
Here, you can have these back, Daisy-chan.

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:02.720
The frames are still warm.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.140
W... W... Wha...

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:06.760
Well then, shall we...

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.600
...introduce ourselves again?

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:15.130
Student Council, General Affairs, 
third-year, Shiba Michiru!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:19.090
The council's secretary, 
second-year, Asahina Kikuno.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.990
So you know, her nickname is Daisy.

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.030
You needn't say things which are unnecessary.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:27.160
Then, that picture was...

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:30.260
We just pretended to shoplift.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.830
Thanks for completely falling for it.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.370
You bastard!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:35.920
D.O.S.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.170
Drown. Out in a. Sewer.

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.680
Ooh, scary.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.890
Good work, everyone.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:45.720
I brought snacks!

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:47.300
There's more of 'em!

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:51.980
Student Council Treasurer, 
second-year, Unyuu Mimori.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:54.360
And I'm just a rank-and-file...

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.800
Why are you lying?

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:56.560
President!

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:59.770
That's me. Agata Soujirou.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.690
I think you people have gone a bit too far.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:05.820
Give yourselves up without a fight.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:12.170
We are the Kaimei Academy Student Council!

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:13.040
<b>Student Council</b>

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.160
And that ends that.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.580
We'll leave the rest to the juvenile 
division of the boys in blue.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:22.500
U-Um...

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:26.340
I'm from the Academy Times! 
Can I ask you some questions?

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.310
Carefully now, Bossun...

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:43.370
Carefully...

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:44.760
Be really, really careful...

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:45.990
Shut up, already!

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:46.820
Finished!

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:49.030
Awesome, Bossun!

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.620
You'll totally be in the 
Guinness Book of World Records!

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:52.560
I name it the Tower of Bossun!

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.280
Lame...

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:54.760
Hurry up, Momoka... Take a picture!

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:55.790
Yes, Ma'am!

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:59.290
Bossman, let her in the picture!

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:01.630
Bossman? But I made it!

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:02.880
Silence!

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:09.010
The Tower of Bossun!

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:10.000
It's fallen to pieces!

00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:12.220
Who did it?! Who?!

00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:14.240
The Student Council.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:16.980
You are the Sket-dan, yes?

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:52.710
I am Tsubaki Sasuke, from 
the Student Council.

00:23:52.710 --> 00:23:54.240
I'm the leader of the Sket-dan, Bossun!

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:54.990
Stop copying me!

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:56.030
And <i>you</i> stop copying <i>me</i>!

00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:57.200
This isn't Sketch Dance!

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:00.750
Heh, heh, heh. You two seem pretty similar.

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:02.460
President, don't compare 
me to someone like him!

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:03.690
That's my line!

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:05.090
Well, in that case...

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:06.250
We'll battle it out!

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.680
Next time: Even Onihime 
Has Tears in Her Eyes.

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:10.800
Hey, don't go deciding that!

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:11.940
You want our special pose?

00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:13.340
Here we go... We are the Student...

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:15.010
Don't copy us! DOS!

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:16.810
We're the academy support group!

00:24:16.810 --> 00:24:18.120
Sket Dance!
